@startuml Complete YesLove System Architecture

!theme plain
skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam handwritten false

actor User as U
participant "Mobile App" as MA
participant "Load Balancer" as LB
participant "Flask API" as API
participant "Auth Service" as AUTH
participant "Feed Service" as FEED
participant "Media Service" as MEDIA
participant "Notification Service" as NOTIF

database "SQLite DB" as DB
database "Redis Cache" as REDIS
database "Amazon Neptune" as NEPTUNE
queue "Amazon SQS" as SQS
participant "SQS Workers" as WORKERS
participant "AWS S3" as S3
participant "CloudFront CDN" as CDN
participant "Firebase FCM" as FCM

== User Authentication & Device Registration ==

U -> MA: Login
MA -> LB: POST /auth/login\n{username, password, device_token, platform}
LB -> API: Route request
API -> AUTH: Process login
AUTH -> DB: Validate user
AUTH -> DB: Store device token
AUTH --> MA: JWT + Success
MA --> U: Logged in

== Post Creation & Fanout ==

U -> MA: Create Post
MA -> API: POST /feed/post\n{content, image}
API -> FEED: Process post
FEED -> DB: Save post
FEED -> MEDIA: Process image (if any)
MEDIA -> S3: Upload to S3
S3 -> CDN: Distribute via CloudFront

FEED -> SQS: Queue fanout job\n{post_id, author_id, follower_ids}
FEED -> NEPTUNE: Update social graph
FEED -> REDIS: Invalidate author's cache

WORKERS -> SQS: Poll for jobs
WORKERS -> REDIS: Invalidate followers' feed cache
WORKERS -> NOTIF: Send push notifications
NOTIF -> FCM: Send to devices
FCM -> MA: Push notification
MA -> U: Show notification

== Feed Retrieval with Caching ==

U -> MA: View Feed
MA -> API: GET /feed?page=1
API -> FEED: Get user feed
FEED -> REDIS: Check cache
alt Cache Hit
    REDIS --> FEED: Return cached feed
else Cache Miss
    FEED -> DB: Query posts from followed users
    FEED -> NEPTUNE: Get social graph data
    FEED -> REDIS: Cache generated feed
end
FEED --> MA: Feed data
MA --> U: Display posts

== Social Interactions ==

U -> MA: Like Post
MA -> API: POST /feed/post/{id}/like
API -> FEED: Process like
FEED -> DB: Save like
FEED -> NOTIF: Queue notification
NOTIF -> SQS: Queue push job
WORKERS -> SQS: Process notification
WORKERS -> FCM: Send to post author
FCM -> MA: Like notification

== Media Upload & Processing ==

U -> MA: Upload Media
MA -> API: POST /media/upload
API -> MEDIA: Process upload
MEDIA -> S3: Store original
MEDIA -> SQS: Queue processing job\n{resize, compress}
WORKERS -> SQS: Process media
WORKERS -> S3: Store processed versions
WORKERS -> CDN: Invalidate cache
MEDIA --> MA: Media URLs

== Event Creation & Notifications ==

U -> MA: Create Event
MA -> API: POST /events/event_info
API -> DB: Save event
API -> NEPTUNE: Update graph relationships
API -> SQS: Queue follower notifications
WORKERS -> NOTIF: Send event notifications
NOTIF -> FCM: Notify followers

== Notification Preferences ==

U -> MA: Update Settings
MA -> API: PUT /notifications/preferences\n{posts: true, likes: false}
API -> DB: Update preferences
note right: Future notifications respect these settings

== Background Processing Flow ==

SQS -> WORKERS: Message polling
WORKERS -> WORKERS: Process job types:\n- Push notifications\n- Media processing\n- Feed fanout\n- Email sending
WORKERS -> DB: Update job status
WORKERS -> REDIS: Cache operations
WORKERS -> FCM: Send notifications
WORKERS -> S3: Media operations

== System Monitoring ==

API -> API: Prometheus metrics
REDIS -> REDIS: Cache hit/miss stats
SQS -> SQS: Queue depth monitoring
WORKERS -> WORKERS: Job processing metrics

note over U, FCM
**Key Improvements:**
- Device tokens auto-managed during auth
- Feed caching with Redis for performance
- Async fanout via SQS workers
- Media processing with S3 + CloudFront
- Neptune for social graph queries
- Granular notification preferences
- Background job processing
end note

@enduml